P0 — Public profiles can display fabricated identities and photos
PublicProfileModal.tsx, lines 61–128.
The new component uses Supabase profiles first, but falls back to seeded profiles or feed-provided identity fields. It also hardcodes a particular user's avatar, biography, city and interests.
This means a public profile can look complete even when its canonical profile was not resolved.
Required correction: Resolve identity through the canonical profile record. Do not manufacture missing personal attributes.
P0 — ECHO and PULL do not yet deliver real cross-account behavior
src/domains/d03_social_graph/index.ts, lines 80–172, and src/domains/d17_matching/index.ts, lines 78–214.
Both implementations persist relationship state in browser localStorage. The newly added sendPull() updates only that local state, not a recipient's authoritative backend inbox.
The UI may show ECHOED or PULLED, but this does not establish that the other account received the action.
Required correction: Use D03 and D17's approved backend authority and verify sender/recipient behavior with two accounts.
P0 — Authentication has contradictory profile-resolution paths
src/lib/auth.tsx, lines 75–119 and 164–190.
The new code adds a hardcoded Auth UUID-to-profile mapping and falls back to profile lookup using editable Auth metadata.
But the explicit login function still performs the older identity-link lookup after hydration. An account can therefore resolve during hydration yet fail the login function's separate profile check.
Required correction: Establish one verified, canonical Auth-to-profile resolution path. Do not select ownership from editable handles or arbitrary client metadata.
P1 — Public-profile lookup can mix two different identities
PublicProfileModal.tsx, lines 61–71.
When both an ID and handle are supplied, the Supabase query uses an OR condition. If they disagree, the query may return an unintended profile or fail because multiple records match.
The component does not establish which identifier is authoritative before opening the profile.
Required correction: Resolve canonical profile ID first; use the handle only as a lookup/display attribute.
P1 — ECHO/PULL actions lack authenticated-user gating
PublicProfileModal.tsx, lines 160–185.
The action handlers do not require a verified current user. They can fall back to the string current_user, allowing local UI relationships that are not tied to a real authenticated principal.
Required correction: Guest users may view public profiles, but relationship writes must require valid authenticated identity.
